    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Flemingsburg was founded in 1797 by George Stockton, who named the town after his half‑brother Colonel John Fleming.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flemingsburg%2C_Kentucky"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Major George Stockton and Colonel John Fleming explored the Ohio River by canoe in 1776, becoming among the first explorers of the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://flemingsburgky.org/community/history.php"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town became the county seat in 1798, shortly after its founding.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://flemingsburgky.org/community/history.php"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A railroad served Flemingsburg until 1956, marking a mid‑20th century link to the wider region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://flemingsburgky.org/community/history.php"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The downtown historic district is currently being renovated into a Covered Bridge Museum with federal transportation funds.",
